 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le01ob12re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Ok class, we covered an interesting topic last class. Who can remind me what we studied yesterday? How about you Victor?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: We worked on the difference between data, information, and knowledge. You told us that we could mix up the three concepts. So, we should be careful when defining each one of them. First, we discussed knowledge. Simply put, knowledge is what we know and is stored in our brains, like a map of the world. Currently, you can only keep knowledge in a human brain. Computers are not artificial brains because they don't understand what they process and can't make independent decisions. Thus, internet is not a network of human knowledge. The brain uses two sources to build knowledge: data and information.</div>", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "53000", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Excellent, Victor. Now, Cristina could you tell me what data is? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Cristina</span>: Data are the facts in reality. For example, your age or your height. Data is a description of the real world as we perceive it with our senses. In the past, humans could only build knowledge of the world by direct experience. Before they started storing data as information, you couldn't know a person's height by looking at a database; you had to measure or ask the person directly. Nowadays, we can store it in computes and check it whenever we want.</div>", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "92000", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Great job Cristina. Finally, Victor can you tell me what information is?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: Information is how humans expand their knowledge beyond the data collected by their senses. In other words, information is the record of data we have of the world. For example, a photograph of you is information on how you look, but your appearance in the real world is data. You can send, transform or even destroy the photograph, but your looks, in reality, are not affected.</br>\n<strong>Teacher:</strong> Very good Victor. OK class; remember you shouldn't confuse the concepts of data, knowledge, and information. For next class, bring some ideas about how these concepts have changed, in the past, we had a different concept of information and data, these days, data, information and knowledge are related one to each other.</div>", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le01ob12re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "image": "", "id": 0}], "video_src": "enpe7n3le01ob12re5vsc01"}, "type": "video"}], "title": "", "id": 2, "type": "video"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}